#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:104
#: 7cd958431bfa4d5d98b98c7995b2dd06
msgid ""
"The twelve H3 subsections below — one per cell, in the fixed order **SDD "
"row, then TDD row, then MDD row** — are the chapter's working body. Every "
"case-study chapter (07–11) scores a real harness against the same twelve "
"cells."
msgstr ""
"下面十二个 H3 小节——每格一节，按 **先 SDD 行、再 TDD 行、最后 MDD 行** "
"的固定顺序排列——是本章的主干。每一章案例研究（07–11）都以同样的十二格为坐标，给一具真实的挽具打分。"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:109
#: 0653fd7c02bb4701b85338e1f91514f2
msgid ""
"A word on how to *read* the matrix. The twelve cells are analytically "
"independent (a strong TDD × Fence does not imply a strong SDD × Groom) but "
"*operationally coupled* — strong cells cover for weak ones, and weak cells "
"quietly sabotage strong ones. Three couplings worth noticing before reading "
"any row:"
msgstr ""
"关于这张矩阵 *应该怎么读*，先说一句。这十二格在分析上彼此独立（一个强壮的 TDD × 护栏并不意味着也会有一个强壮的 SDD × 梳理），但在 "
"*操作* 上彼此耦合——强的格子会替弱的格子顶住一阵，弱的格子也会无声地拖垮强的格子。在读任何一行之前，有三种耦合值得先注意："

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:115
#: fcece7fa8c124292904058b56bb1ad7e
msgid ""
"**Bridle weakness amplifies through Fence strength.** A vague `AGENTS.md` "
"(weak SDD × Bridle) paired with a strict pre-commit hook (strong TDD × "
"Fence) produces code that is *clean* and *wrong*: the lint passes, the tests"
" pass, and the architecture violates the intent the spec never pinned down. "
"Strong fences make weak bridles invisible — until the architectural debt "
"surfaces in an incident."
msgstr ""
"**缰绳的弱，会被护栏的强放大出来。** 一份含糊的 `AGENTS.md`（SDD × 缰绳弱）搭配一条严苛的 pre-commit 钩子（TDD ×"
" 护栏强），会产出那种 *干净而错* 的代码：lint "
"过了、测试过了，而架构违反着规约从未钉住的那份意图。强壮的护栏让虚弱的缰绳看起来像没事——直到架构债在一场事故里浮出水面。"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:121
#: 22bee1f1a8ba4afe8af7b7fc525ceeec
msgid ""
"**Paddock strength hides Bridle weakness.** A thorough PR review ritual "
"(strong SDD × Paddock) can carry a team for a year with a mediocre "
"`AGENTS.md`, because the human reviewer compensates on every merge. The "
"weakness appears the moment the team scales reviewer capacity less than it "
"scales agent output — which is *always*."
msgstr ""
"**牧场的强，会掩盖缰绳的弱。** 一套扎实的 PR 评审仪式（SDD × 牧场强），在一份平庸的 `AGENTS.md` "
"下也能把团队扛上一年，因为每一次合并都靠评审人顶上来。一旦团队\"扩评审人能力\"的速度慢于\"扩智能体产出\"的速度，这份弱就暴露出来——而这永远会发生。"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:126
#: 04b231a0e05b40929b37c526ec803be5
msgid ""
"**Groom is where the other three decay.** Every cell in the Bridle, Fence, "
"and Paddock columns depreciates by default; the Groom column is what pays "
"the depreciation down. A harness with zeros in the Groom column will drift "
"back to zeros in every other column within two quarters, regardless of how "
"much was invested up front."
msgstr ""
"**梳理是其他三列衰减的归宿。** "
"缰绳、护栏、牧场这三列上的每一格，默认都在贬值；梳理这一列存在的意义，就是把这份折旧偿还下去。一具梳理列为零的挽具，不管开始时投入了多少，都会在两个季度内把其他三列的分数都拖回零。"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:132
#: dfa5d3de7da640619a433de065b61afd
msgid ""
"Read each cell below with this coupling in mind: a high score is not durable"
" without its sibling cells, and no single cell is load-bearing on its own."
msgstr "读下面每一格时，把这种耦合放在心里：一个高分若没有兄弟格子陪着，并不耐用；没有哪一格能独自承重。"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:137
#: c5b62c61741b4ec8a5ee1025e64ffba7
msgid "SDD × Bridle — Agent-facing specs that steer"
msgstr "SDD × 缰绳 —— 引导智能体的规约"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:139
#: 331024b67f7340e28731c100ce5c67a2
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Definition.** A bridle in this cell is any file the agent *reads before it"
" writes anything* and whose primary purpose is to shape what the agent tries"
" to build. `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, and top-level `SKILL.md` files live "
"here {cite}`anthropic2024claudecode`. A bridle that is unread or stale "
"steers nothing; the guardian responsibility therefore extends to keeping the"
" file fresh, not merely present."
msgstr ""
"**定义。** 这一格里的缰绳，指的是智能体 *在动笔之前会先读* "
"的任何一份文件，它的首要目的是塑造\"智能体试图去建什么\"。`AGENTS.md`、`CLAUDE.md`、顶层的 `SKILL.md` 都住在这里 "
"{cite}`anthropic2024claudecode`。一份没人读或已经过时的缰绳，什么也引导不了；因此这位护法的职责不止是让文件在场，更要让它保持新鲜。"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:146
#: f51f21dc9d9d4cd886cc814b610146d3
msgid ""
"<!-- verified: 2026-04-17 · SDD × Bridle · agent-facing spec that steers before writing -->\n"
"\n"
"# AGENTS.md — sample\n"
"\n"
"## Role & Scope\n"
"You are a coding agent for `todo-cli`. You may edit files under `todo/` and\n"
"`tests/`. You must not touch `scripts/`, `deploy/`, or any `.env*` file.\n"
"\n"
"## House rules\n"
"- Before editing any file, list `tests/test_<basename>.py`; if it exists, read it.\n"
"- Never invent package names; use the pinned versions in `pyproject.toml`.\n"
"- Every new public function gets a docstring and a test; no exceptions.\n"
"\n"
"## Escalation\n"
"If a rule above conflicts with user instruction, pause and surface the\n"
"conflict explicitly; do not silently override.\n"
msgstr ""
"<!-- verified: 2026-04-17 · SDD × Bridle · agent-facing spec that steers before writing -->\n"
"\n"
"# AGENTS.md — sample\n"
"\n"
"## Role & Scope\n"
"You are a coding agent for `todo-cli`. You may edit files under `todo/` and\n"
"`tests/`. You must not touch `scripts/`, `deploy/`, or any `.env*` file.\n"
"\n"
"## House rules\n"
"- Before editing any file, list `tests/test_<basename>.py`; if it exists, read it.\n"
"- Never invent package names; use the pinned versions in `pyproject.toml`.\n"
"- Every new public function gets a docstring and a test; no exceptions.\n"
"\n"
"## Escalation\n"
"If a rule above conflicts with user instruction, pause and surface the\n"
"conflict explicitly; do not silently override.\n"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:151
#: d97c252a0b864c3bba6feebc8a58dc11
msgid "SDD × Fence — Spec validity enforced at the gate"
msgstr "SDD × 护栏 —— 在关卡处强制规约合法性"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:153
#: 4d082d13314441758c1e4f4e73c7c2ce
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Definition.** A fence in this cell enforces that every spec-shaped "
"artefact is *well-formed before it becomes authoritative*. Examples: JSON-"
"Schema validation of prompt templates at commit time, MCP-manifest schema "
"checks, CI steps that refuse documentation builds with unresolved `{ref}` "
"links {cite}`martraire2019living`. Without this fence, spec rot accumulates "
"silently and SDD × Bridle becomes a lie."
msgstr ""
"**定义。** 这一格里的护栏，强制每一件形如\"规约\"的制品，*在它变成权威之前* 就必须格式良好。例如：提示词模板在 commit 时被 "
"JSON-Schema 校验、MCP manifest 的 schema 检查、CI 阶段拒绝包含未解析 `{ref}` 链接的文档构建 "
"{cite}`martraire2019living`。没有这道护栏，规约的腐烂会无声累积，SDD × 缰绳就会沦为一句谎话。"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:160
#: c44fb0bf82a84b3f9bf9e2f90bf8c930
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"$comment\": \"verified: 2026-04-17 · SDD x Fence · JSON Schema validated at commit time\",\n"
"  \"$schema\": \"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\n"
"  \"title\": \"PromptTemplate\",\n"
"  \"type\": \"object\",\n"
"  \"required\": [\"name\", \"system_prompt\", \"user_prompt\", \"tags\"],\n"
"  \"properties\": {\n"
"    \"name\":          {\"type\": \"string\", \"pattern\": \"^[a-z][a-z0-9_]{2,63}$\"},\n"
"    \"system_prompt\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 16},\n"
"    \"user_prompt\":   {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 16},\n"
"    \"tags\":          {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"minItems\": 1}\n"
"  },\n"
"  \"additionalProperties\": false\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""
"{\n"
"  \"$comment\": \"verified: 2026-04-17 · SDD x Fence · JSON Schema validated at commit time\",\n"
"  \"$schema\": \"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\n"
"  \"title\": \"PromptTemplate\",\n"
"  \"type\": \"object\",\n"
"  \"required\": [\"name\", \"system_prompt\", \"user_prompt\", \"tags\"],\n"
"  \"properties\": {\n"
"    \"name\":          {\"type\": \"string\", \"pattern\": \"^[a-z][a-z0-9_]{2,63}$\"},\n"
"    \"system_prompt\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 16},\n"
"    \"user_prompt\":   {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 16},\n"
"    \"tags\":          {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"minItems\": 1}\n"
"  },\n"
"  \"additionalProperties\": false\n"
"}\n"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:165
#: 0305f49c33df4b2abc5449cd0763d372
msgid "SDD × Paddock — Acceptance that matches the spec"
msgstr "SDD × 牧场 —— 与规约相符的验收"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:167
#: 9ea5ea23fd9e45f39f27c4a1f68e9008
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Definition.** A paddock in this cell is a bounded *review ritual* that "
"confirms delivered work matches the spec, role by role, line by line. "
"Executable specifications {cite}`adzic2011specbyexample` are the canonical "
"form; the lazy-scrum-team *Verification Table* pattern "
"{cite}`lazyscrumteam2026` is a concrete instance the book adopts throughout."
msgstr ""
"**定义。** 这一格里的牧场，是一场有边界的 *评审仪式*，逐角色、逐行地确认\"交付的工作与规约相符\"。可执行规约 "
"{cite}`adzic2011specbyexample` 是它的经典形态；lazy-scrum-team 的 *验证表（Verification "
"Table）* 模式 {cite}`lazyscrumteam2026` 是本书全程采用的一个具体实例。"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:174
#: a5dca9ec08514a7a8f6350f2eea59231
msgid ""
"<!-- verified: 2026-04-17 · SDD × Paddock · Verification Table pattern from lazy-scrum-team -->\n"
"\n"
"# Acceptance Gate — Verification Table\n"
"\n"
"A story is `done` only when every row below is checked by the named role.\n"
"\n"
"| # | Requirement                          | Evidence (file or URL)       | Checked by        |\n"
"|---|--------------------------------------|------------------------------|-------------------|\n"
"| 1 | Acceptance tests green               | CI run link                  | Test Engineer     |\n"
"| 2 | `AGENTS.md` rules unchanged or versioned | `git diff` summary       | Architect         |\n"
"| 3 | `CHANGELOG.md` entry under Unreleased | diff hunk                   | PO                |\n"
"| 4 | No new TODO/FIXME markers added      | `rg -c TODO` before/after    | Code Reviewer     |\n"
"| 5 | HarnessCard cell score unchanged or explained | HarnessCard delta note | Final Acceptance  |\n"
"\n"
"Rows may only be marked by the named role; self-certification is rejected.\n"
msgstr ""
"<!-- verified: 2026-04-17 · SDD × Paddock · Verification Table pattern from lazy-scrum-team -->\n"
"\n"
"# 验收关卡 —— 验证表\n"
"\n"
"只有下表每一行都被对应角色打勾，一个故事才算 `done`。\n"
"\n"
"| # | 需求                                  | 证据（文件或 URL）              | 签字人             |\n"
"|---|---------------------------------------|-------------------------------|-------------------|\n"
"| 1 | 验收测试变绿                           | CI 跑动链接                    | Test Engineer     |\n"
"| 2 | `AGENTS.md` 规则未变、或已版本化        | `git diff` 摘要                | Architect         |\n"
"| 3 | `CHANGELOG.md` 在 Unreleased 下有条目   | diff 片段                      | PO                |\n"
"| 4 | 无新增 TODO/FIXME 标记                 | `rg -c TODO` 前后对比           | Code Reviewer     |\n"
"| 5 | HarnessCard 格子分数不变，或有说明      | HarnessCard delta 备注         | Final Acceptance  |\n"
"\n"
"每一行只能由署名的角色来打勾；自证不被接受。\n"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:179
#: 54f18f5a3279469b889b352511f54b5b
msgid "SDD × Groom — Keeping the spec surface alive"
msgstr "SDD × 梳理 —— 让规约面持续鲜活"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:181
#: a7ce80f1bf704180846869849dffbb9f
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Definition.** A groom action in this cell is a *recurring maintenance job*"
" that refreshes the spec surface so the agent's input never silently rots. "
"Broken-link sweeps, stale `verified:` header rewrites, and weekly "
"regeneration of auto-generated `AGENTS.md` tables of contents are typical "
"{cite}`ford2017buildingevolutionary`. Without grooming, SDD entropy "
"accumulates faster than authors can keep up."
msgstr ""
"**定义。** 这一格里的梳理动作，是一项 *反复运行的维护作业*，用来刷新规约面，以使智能体的输入永远不会悄无声息地腐烂。典型做法：扫坏链、重写过期的"
" `verified:` 头、每周重新生成自动化 `AGENTS.md` 目录 "
"{cite}`ford2017buildingevolutionary`。没有梳理，SDD 的熵累积速度会快过作者跟得上的速度。"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:188
#: 65febb0b95944ffaba540a2dac66f312
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n"
"# verified: 2026-04-17 · SDD × Groom · weekly doc-sync job\n"
"# Refreshes living documentation so the spec surface the agent reads does\n"
"# not silently drift from the code it describes.\n"
"set -euo pipefail\n"
"\n"
"make book-linkcheck || echo \"::warning::broken links surfaced\"\n"
"\n"
"# regenerate AGENTS.md TOC from source chapters\n"
"python scripts/gen_agents_toc.py > AGENTS.md.next\n"
"diff -u AGENTS.md AGENTS.md.next && rm AGENTS.md.next \\\n"
"  || { mv AGENTS.md.next AGENTS.md; git add AGENTS.md; }\n"
"\n"
"# re-stamp `verified:` headers in _handson/ artefacts modified this week\n"
"python scripts/restamp_verified.py book/source/_handson\n"
msgstr ""
"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n"
"# verified: 2026-04-17 · SDD × Groom · weekly doc-sync job\n"
"# Refreshes living documentation so the spec surface the agent reads does\n"
"# not silently drift from the code it describes.\n"
"set -euo pipefail\n"
"\n"
"make book-linkcheck || echo \"::warning::broken links surfaced\"\n"
"\n"
"# regenerate AGENTS.md TOC from source chapters\n"
"python scripts/gen_agents_toc.py > AGENTS.md.next\n"
"diff -u AGENTS.md AGENTS.md.next && rm AGENTS.md.next \\\n"
"  || { mv AGENTS.md.next AGENTS.md; git add AGENTS.md; }\n"
"\n"
"# re-stamp `verified:` headers in _handson/ artefacts modified this week\n"
"python scripts/restamp_verified.py book/source/_handson\n"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:192
#: 1d9d22a5616c47638780ea0600d39486
msgid "Pitfall — SDD row failure modes"
msgstr "陷阱——SDD 行的失败模式"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:195
#: c62cdabf9af34e4ab67c2343fd007499
msgid ""
"The SDD row's distinctive failure is not *absence* of specs but "
"*unfalsifiable* ones. Two cell-specific variants worth naming (Ch.03's "
"*aspirational `CLAUDE.md`* edge case covers the third):"
msgstr ""
"SDD 行的特异失败，不是规约 *缺席*，而是规约 *无法被证伪*。有两种按格子分的变体值得点名（第三种——\"愿望型 "
"`CLAUDE.md`\"，已经被第 03 章覆盖）："

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:199
#: c8a0825373514c06b5c319ddc47ec013
msgid ""
"**The MCP manifest that outlives its handler.** The schema advertises a tool"
" the server no longer implements; the agent invokes it confidently and "
"receives a puzzling error. SDD × Fence exists to catch exactly this, but "
"only if the fence is wired to *both* sides of the schema-to-handler "
"contract."
msgstr ""
"**比 handler 活得还久的 MCP manifest。** schema "
"里写着一个服务器早已不再实现的工具；智能体自信地调用它，得到一条莫名其妙的错误。SDD × 护栏正是为了抓这种失败而存在的，但前提是这道护栏 *两端* "
"都要被接上\"schema－handler\"契约的两头。"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:204
#: 6b27579b9d3348bca599ba0d5a0870d6
msgid ""
"**The unversioned spec.** `AGENTS.md` with no changelog, no `verified:` "
"date, no sign of having evolved. Reviewers cannot tell whether its claims "
"are current or legacy; agent and human both read it as authoritative. SDD × "
"Groom is the answer — but only if the Groom job fails loudly when the spec "
"has not been touched in N weeks."
msgstr ""
"**没有版本的规约。** 一份 `AGENTS.md`，没有 changelog、没有 `verified:` "
"日期、看不出被演进过。评审者判断不出里面的主张是当下的还是遗留的；智能体和人都把它当作权威来读。SDD × 梳理是答案——但前提是，当规约 N "
"周没被碰过时，这项梳理作业会大声失败。"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:211
#: 8bb29a6bd6a344bea9a5a5ce24d0ef18
msgid ""
"Row-level test: can you name, for each SDD cell, one artefact in your repo "
"today and one check that would fire *this week* if it broke? If any cell's "
"answer is \"we trust people to keep it current\", that cell is at zero "
"regardless of the file contents."
msgstr ""
"行级自测：针对 SDD 的每一格，你都能点出今天仓库里对应的一件制品、以及一条若它坏掉会在 *本周之内* "
"触发的检查吗？哪一格的答案若是\"我们相信大家会把它保持新鲜\"，那无论那一格里的文件内容多好，它的分数都是零。"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:218
#: 77c10217b7be4ea4bd2e9ec6dcde3128
msgid "TDD × Bridle — Failing-first tests as input to the agent"
msgstr "TDD × 缰绳 —— 先失败的测试作为给智能体的输入"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:220
#: 5bfcdbd55b124e198bc0bc4431157167
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Definition.** A bridle in this cell is a *deliberately red test suite* "
"committed before the agent is invited in. The agent reads the failing tests "
"as part of its context and understands *what it must make green* before "
"writing production code {cite}`beck2002tdd`. The key property is *red on "
"commit*, not \"a test exists somewhere\"."
msgstr ""
"**定义。** 这一格里的缰绳，是一份 *故意为红* "
"的测试套件，在智能体被请进来之前就先提交进仓库。智能体把这些失败的测试作为上下文的一部分读进来，从而明白 *在它动手写生产代码之前，必须把哪些测试变绿*"
" {cite}`beck2002tdd`。关键性质是\"commit 时是红的\"，而不是\"某处存在着一条测试\"。"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:226
#: bdcfd6090b544e47a71ab2be6a590125
msgid ""
"# verified: 2026-04-17 · TDD × Bridle · starter tests steer the agent before it writes\n"
"\"\"\"A minimal failing-first suite that pins the agent loop shape.\n"
"\n"
"Committing this file before the first prompt means the agent cannot fake\n"
"progress: a turn that does not green one of these tests did not advance\n"
"the project.\n"
"\"\"\"\n"
"import pytest\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"def test_loop_halts_on_empty_plan(loop):\n"
"    assert loop.step(plan=[]) == \"halt\"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"def test_loop_consumes_one_tool_call_per_step(loop):\n"
"    result = loop.step(plan=[\"noop_tool\"])\n"
"    assert result.tool_calls == 1\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"@pytest.fixture\n"
"def loop():\n"
"    from todo.agent import AgentLoop\n"
"    return AgentLoop()\n"
msgstr ""
"# verified: 2026-04-17 · TDD × Bridle · starter tests steer the agent before it writes\n"
"\"\"\"A minimal failing-first suite that pins the agent loop shape.\n"
"\n"
"Committing this file before the first prompt means the agent cannot fake\n"
"progress: a turn that does not green one of these tests did not advance\n"
"the project.\n"
"\"\"\"\n"
"import pytest\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"def test_loop_halts_on_empty_plan(loop):\n"
"    assert loop.step(plan=[]) == \"halt\"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"def test_loop_consumes_one_tool_call_per_step(loop):\n"
"    result = loop.step(plan=[\"noop_tool\"])\n"
"    assert result.tool_calls == 1\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"@pytest.fixture\n"
"def loop():\n"
"    from todo.agent import AgentLoop\n"
"    return AgentLoop()\n"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:231
#: dd1c0e90365344e586543787ab058ca9
msgid "TDD × Fence — Hooks that refuse red-tree commits"
msgstr "TDD × 护栏 —— 拒绝红树 commit 的钩子"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:233
#: ad9736338aaf456f84d7a54a85287cce
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Definition.** A fence in this cell blocks any edit or commit while the "
"test tree is red. Pre-commit hooks, Claude-Code `PreToolUse` hooks, and "
"required CI checks all belong here {cite}`humble2010continuousdelivery`. The"
" distinction from TDD × Paddock is *immediacy* — a TDD fence fires at the "
"keystroke, a TDD paddock fires at the PR."
msgstr ""
"**定义。** 这一格里的护栏，会在测试树为红时拦住任何修改或 commit。pre-commit 钩子、Claude-Code 的 "
"`PreToolUse` 钩子、以及必过的 CI 检查都属于这里 {cite}`humble2010continuousdelivery`。它和 TDD"
" × 牧场的区别在于 *及时性*——TDD 护栏在键盘敲击那一刻就触发，TDD 牧场在 PR 那一刻才触发。"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:239
#: 7ca44f218c124fa38300e2af7d35131f
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"$comment\": \"verified: 2026-04-17 · TDD x Fence · Claude Code hook blocks on red tests\",\n"
"  \"hooks\": {\n"
"    \"PreToolUse\": [\n"
"      {\"matcher\": \"Write|Edit|MultiEdit\", \"command\": \"pytest -q -m 'not slow'\",\n"
"       \"stopOnFailure\": true, \"description\": \"refuse edits while tests are red\"}\n"
"    ],\n"
"    \"PostToolUse\": [\n"
"      {\"matcher\": \"Write|Edit|MultiEdit\", \"command\": \"ruff check .\",\n"
"       \"stopOnFailure\": false}\n"
"    ]\n"
"  }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""
"{\n"
"  \"$comment\": \"verified: 2026-04-17 · TDD x Fence · Claude Code hook blocks on red tests\",\n"
"  \"hooks\": {\n"
"    \"PreToolUse\": [\n"
"      {\"matcher\": \"Write|Edit|MultiEdit\", \"command\": \"pytest -q -m 'not slow'\",\n"
"       \"stopOnFailure\": true, \"description\": \"refuse edits while tests are red\"}\n"
"    ],\n"
"    \"PostToolUse\": [\n"
"      {\"matcher\": \"Write|Edit|MultiEdit\", \"command\": \"ruff check .\",\n"
"       \"stopOnFailure\": false}\n"
"    ]\n"
"  }\n"
"}\n"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:244
#: 44320bc9b1e84981afbd4850e8f44081
msgid "TDD × Paddock — CI gate and environment parity"
msgstr "TDD × 牧场 —— CI 关卡与环境对等"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:246
#: 8b7b328b3358493db902eb458533d2ce
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Definition.** A paddock in this cell is a *required, branch-protected test"
" run* that happens in an environment faithful to production. It is the "
"integration-level twin of TDD × Fence: broader in scope, slower in "
"turnaround, authoritative in verdict {cite}`forsgren2018accelerate`."
msgstr ""
"**定义。** 这一格里的牧场，是一次 *必过、分支保护下* 的测试运行，发生在一个忠实于生产环境的环境中。它是 TDD × "
"护栏在集成层面上的孪生兄弟：覆盖更广、周转更慢、判决更权威 {cite}`forsgren2018accelerate`。"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:251
#: a5be0f8876944b56a37a4bc437129071
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"# verified: 2026-04-17 · TDD × Paddock · required status check on protected branch\n"
"name: ci-gate\n"
"on: [pull_request]\n"
"jobs:\n"
"  test:\n"
"    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n"
"    steps:\n"
"      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n"
"      - uses: actions/setup-python@v5\n"
"        with: {python-version: \"3.11\"}\n"
"      - run: pip install -e \".[test]\"\n"
"      - run: pytest -q --junitxml=junit.xml\n"
"      - if: failure()\n"
"        run: echo \"::error::gate failed — branch cannot merge\"\n"
msgstr ""
"# verified: 2026-04-17 · TDD × Paddock · required status check on protected branch\n"
"name: ci-gate\n"
"on: [pull_request]\n"
"jobs:\n"
"  test:\n"
"    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n"
"    steps:\n"
"      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n"
"      - uses: actions/setup-python@v5\n"
"        with: {python-version: \"3.11\"}\n"
"      - run: pip install -e \".[test]\"\n"
"      - run: pytest -q --junitxml=junit.xml\n"
"      - if: failure()\n"
"        run: echo \"::error::gate failed — branch cannot merge\"\n"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:256
#: 7cc508b47b094254976f492219c8dd67
msgid "TDD × Groom — Flake maintenance and test-surface evolution"
msgstr "TDD × 梳理 —— flake 维护与测试面演进"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:258
#: ddae12336bdb43b2983f5870e199be0a
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Definition.** A groom action in this cell is a *recurring policy* for "
"handling tests that stop being load-bearing — flakes, long-extinct "
"regressions, tests that drift out of step with the spec they verified. "
"Without grooming, the test corpus accumulates dead weight and eventually "
"*loses* the team's trust {cite}`cunningham1992debt`."
msgstr ""
"**定义。** 这一格里的梳理动作，是一套处理\"不再承重的测试\"的 "
"*反复政策*——flake、早已消失的回归、以及与它当初所核验的那份规约脱节的测试。没有梳理，测试语料会不断累积死重，最终 *失去* 团队的信任 "
"{cite}`cunningham1992debt`。"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:264
#: c352d1827219496bb2d23cd22541ba67
msgid ""
"<!-- verified: 2026-04-17 · TDD × Groom · flaky-test quarantine policy -->\n"
"\n"
"# Flaky Test Quarantine\n"
"\n"
"A test that fails intermittently without a code change enters quarantine:\n"
"\n"
"1. Move it from `tests/` into `tests/quarantine/`; mark with `@pytest.mark.flaky`.\n"
"2. Open an issue tagged `quarantine` with the last three failure logs.\n"
"3. CI runs `tests/quarantine/` separately; failures post a comment but do\n"
"   not block the merge.\n"
"4. If the quarantined test is green for 7 consecutive nightly runs, promote\n"
"   it back into `tests/`; if red for 30 days, delete with an explicit\n"
"   justification in the commit message.\n"
"\n"
"Quarantine is a paddock *inside* the paddock: a space where flakes cannot\n"
"poison the main gate while still being tracked.\n"
msgstr ""
"<!-- verified: 2026-04-17 · TDD × Groom · flaky-test quarantine policy -->\n"
"\n"
"# Flaky 测试隔离区\n"
"\n"
"一条在没有代码变更的情况下偶尔失败的测试，进入隔离区：\n"
"\n"
"1. 把它从 `tests/` 移到 `tests/quarantine/`；用 `@pytest.mark.flaky` 标注。\n"
"2. 开一个带 `quarantine` 标签的 issue，附上最近三次失败日志。\n"
"3. CI 单独跑 `tests/quarantine/`；失败会留一条评论，但\n"
"   不会阻塞合并。\n"
"4. 若这条被隔离的测试连续 7 次夜间构建都为绿，把它提升回 `tests/`；若\n"
"   连续 30 天为红，在 commit message 里写明理由后删除它。\n"
"\n"
"隔离区是 *牧场里的牧场*：一个让 flake 既不污染主关卡、\n"
"又仍然被跟踪的空间。\n"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:268
#: 41d0d10704f94543897b7543aeb56826
msgid "Pitfall — TDD row failure modes"
msgstr "陷阱——TDD 行的失败模式"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:271
#: 61b6c824f4b740b18f2efb75183d2450
msgid ""
"The TDD row fails in ways the SDD row does not, because tests have an "
"unusual property: a failing test is *cheap*, but a *passing test that has "
"lost contact with the behaviour it verifies* is worse than no test. Three "
"row-level failures:"
msgstr ""
"TDD 行的失败方式，跟 SDD 行不同，因为测试有一项不寻常的性质：一条失败的测试 *便宜*；而一条 "
"*仍然通过、但已经与它核验的那份行为失联的测试*，比没有测试还糟。三种行级失败："

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:276
#: c8dea89b40614de6b1f403839d1ca61a
msgid ""
"**The red-but-ignored test.** A flaky test fails once a week; someone adds "
"`@pytest.mark.skip(\"flaky, fix later\")`; \"later\" never comes. The test "
"now consumes CI cycles, pollutes the output, and teaches the team that red "
"is ignorable — the opposite of TDD × Fence's purpose. If a test is not "
"trusted enough to block a commit, it is not trusted enough to live in the "
"main suite. Move it to quarantine with a dated owner or delete it."
msgstr ""
"**红却被忽略的测试。** 一条 flaky 测试每周失败一次；有人加了 `@pytest.mark.skip(\"flaky, fix "
"later\")`；那个\"later\"永远不会来。这条测试如今在消耗 CI 周期、污染输出，并教会团队\"红是可以忽略的\"——这恰恰是 TDD ×"
" 护栏存在目的的反面。如果一条测试被信任不到能挡住 commit 的程度，那它也配不上住在主测试套件里。把它挪进隔离区、署名指定一位 "
"owner、写上日期，否则就删了。"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:283
#: 3f6d788154da48c6940bf037068b3089
msgid ""
"**The green-and-stale test.** A test pins behaviour the product requirement "
"removed two quarters ago. Nobody notices because it stays green. An agent "
"reading the test as part of TDD × Bridle now learns a *wrong* contract and "
"writes new code against it. Green alone is not evidence of relevance; Groom "
"must periodically ask *which spec does each test now correspond to, and is "
"that spec still live?*"
msgstr ""
"**绿且过期的测试。** 一条测试钉的是两个季度前产品需求早已移除的行为。没人注意到，因为它一直是绿的。一位在 TDD × "
"缰绳框架下读这条测试的智能体，如今学到的是一份 *错误的* "
"契约，然后照着它写新代码。绿本身不等于相关；梳理必须周期性地问：*每一条测试现在对应的是哪一条规约，那条规约还活着吗？*"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:290
#: b2ca21a3596c485f80578b4d7bb06c4a
msgid ""
"**The adversarial test that never got written.** The test the human-authored"
" test *should* have been is the one that would have found the agent's "
"shortcut. If PRs never add \"one more test that attacks the cheapest path to"
" green\" (see Ch.04's first-try-pass pitfall), TDD × Paddock slowly trains "
"the agent rather than guarding against it."
msgstr ""
"**那条从来没被写出来的敌意测试。** 那条人本 *应该* 写但没写的测试，正是能找出智能体捷径的那条。若 PR "
"里从不追加\"再写一条专门攻击通向绿的最省力路径的测试\"（参见第 04 章\"第一把就过\"那条陷阱），TDD × 牧场就会慢慢地 *训练* "
"智能体，而不是防它。"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:297
#: 3fb458239d024fb188eef4160b807e6d
msgid ""
"Row-level test: does your team's test-to-LOC ratio *increase* after AI-"
"assisted PRs, or stay flat? If it stays flat, you are under- investing in "
"the test side of the red-green loop at the precise moment the loop is "
"cheapest to run."
msgstr ""
"行级自测：AI 辅助的 PR 之后，你团队的\"测试／LOC\"比例 *上升* "
"了，还是没动？如果没动，那你正是在这条红—绿循环最便宜的时刻，对循环的测试一侧投入不足。"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:304
#: 7f33a0bd646b4f22a67034549bc307e5
msgid "MDD × Bridle — The one metric that steers"
msgstr "MDD × 缰绳 —— 真正在引导的那一个度量"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:306
#: 9546fbaf268843a68f5cc55d840750b1
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Definition.** A bridle in this cell is a *north-star metric* named before "
"production traffic hits the system. Everything else is diagnostic. The "
"canonical candidate for an AI coding harness is **mean agent turns to "
"green** on a fixed benchmark suite {cite}`langchain2026tbench`."
msgstr ""
"**定义。** 这一格里的缰绳，是一条在生产流量打到系统上之前 *就已被命名* 的 *北极星度量*。其他的一切都是诊断性的。对一具 AI "
"编码挽具而言，经典候选是：在一份固定基准套件上的 **智能体 mean turns to "
"green**（平均变绿轮数）{cite}`langchain2026tbench`。"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:312
#: 94ea4069873043c1b1841494fdd30f8b
msgid ""
"<!-- verified: 2026-04-17 · MDD × Bridle · the one metric that steers -->\n"
"\n"
"# Metrics North-Star\n"
"\n"
"Pick exactly one metric that captures *fitness for purpose* of the harness\n"
"itself, then let every other metric be diagnostic of that one.\n"
"\n"
"- **Project-level north-star:** **mean agent turns to green** on a fixed\n"
"  benchmark suite, measured weekly.\n"
"- **Why:** rising turns-to-green is the earliest observable signal that\n"
"  spec (SDD), tests (TDD), or tooling (MDD) has silently degraded.\n"
"- **Diagnostic metrics** (each tied to a guardian):\n"
"  - SDD — stale `verified:` header count, broken links in `AGENTS.md`\n"
"  - TDD — flaky-test count, coverage floor\n"
"  - MDD — cost per turn, prompt cache hit rate\n"
msgstr ""
"<!-- verified: 2026-04-17 · MDD × Bridle · the one metric that steers -->\n"
"\n"
"# 度量 · 北极星\n"
"\n"
"恰好挑一条能捕捉挽具 *本身是否适配其目的（fitness for purpose）* 的度量，\n"
"然后让其他所有度量都作为这一条的诊断。\n"
"\n"
"- **项目级北极星：** 在一份固定基准套件上的 **智能体 mean turns to green**\n"
"  （平均变绿轮数），每周测一次。\n"
"- **为什么：** turns-to-green 的上升，是规约（SDD）、测试（TDD）、\n"
"  或工具（MDD）已经悄悄退化的最早可观测信号。\n"
"- **诊断度量**（每一条绑一位护法）：\n"
"  - SDD —— 过期 `verified:` 头数量、`AGENTS.md` 里的坏链数\n"
"  - TDD —— flaky 测试数、覆盖率下限\n"
"  - MDD —— 每轮成本、提示词缓存命中率\n"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:317
#: 17f4988c015a45abb02350243e8b7bd2
msgid "MDD × Fence — Cost caps and circuit breakers"
msgstr "MDD × 护栏 —— 成本上限与熔断器"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:319
#: 76800c35736d400c94a1bfd3f026a765
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Definition.** A fence in this cell is an *automated refusal* the moment an"
" observed cost, latency, or error-rate signal crosses a pre-declared "
"threshold. Cost caps on LLM calls, rate limits on tool invocations, and "
"soft/hard kill-switches are typical {cite}`majors2022observability`."
msgstr ""
"**定义。** 这一格里的护栏，是在\"被观测到的成本、延迟、或错误率信号越过预先声明的阈值\"那一刻的 *自动化拒绝*。LLM "
"调用上的成本上限、工具调用的限流、以及软／硬关闭开关都是典型做法 {cite}`majors2022observability`。"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:324
#: ff44322918154fbba9f5d333b855ae8f
msgid ""
"# verified: 2026-04-17 · MDD × Fence · budget circuit-breaker, rejected over limit\n"
"cost_cap_version: \"0.1\"\n"
"per_session_usd:   2.00\n"
"per_day_usd:       50.00\n"
"per_month_usd:     800.00\n"
"action_on_breach:\n"
"  soft: warn_in_status_line\n"
"  hard: refuse_new_tool_calls_until_reset\n"
"alerts:\n"
"  - channel: slack\n"
"    at: 0.75  # of the monthly cap\n"
"  - channel: email\n"
"    at: 0.95\n"
msgstr ""
"# verified: 2026-04-17 · MDD × Fence · budget circuit-breaker, rejected over limit\n"
"cost_cap_version: \"0.1\"\n"
"per_session_usd:   2.00\n"
"per_day_usd:       50.00\n"
"per_month_usd:     800.00\n"
"action_on_breach:\n"
"  soft: warn_in_status_line\n"
"  hard: refuse_new_tool_calls_until_reset\n"
"alerts:\n"
"  - channel: slack\n"
"    at: 0.75  # of the monthly cap\n"
"  - channel: email\n"
"    at: 0.95\n"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:329
#: 71485decf46743a4bc84251e7157ce1a
msgid "MDD × Paddock — Release SLIs and staging soak"
msgstr "MDD × 牧场 —— 发布 SLI 与 staging 浸泡"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:331
#: 602eb75f53b945428289cf1b780d5fdf
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Definition.** A paddock in this cell is a *release gate* that requires "
"production-equivalent signals to hold over a bounded staging window before "
"the bits are allowed to graduate {cite}`ford2017buildingevolutionary`. The "
"window itself is the paddock; the SLIs are the fence at its edge."
msgstr ""
"**定义。** 这一格里的牧场，是一道 *发布关卡*：要求\"等价于生产的信号\"在一个有界的 staging 窗口里都达标，之后这批二进制才被允许毕业"
" {cite}`ford2017buildingevolutionary`。窗口本身是牧场；窗口边上的 SLI，则是这道护栏。"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:336
#: a71d0da62c9543c783ed26269b6ce6cc
msgid ""
"<!-- verified: 2026-04-17 · MDD × Paddock · pre-release SLI gate -->\n"
"\n"
"# Release SLI Gate\n"
"\n"
"A release candidate is blocked from production until these SLIs meet their\n"
"targets for a rolling 24h window in staging:\n"
"\n"
"| SLI                        | Target       | Window  |\n"
"|----------------------------|--------------|---------|\n"
"| p99 latency (user paths)   | ≤ 400 ms     | 24h     |\n"
"| error rate                 | ≤ 0.1 %      | 24h     |\n"
"| harness-internal cost/turn | ≤ $0.03      | 24h     |\n"
"| spec-vs-prod drift score   | ≤ 2 findings | 24h     |\n"
"\n"
"The paddock is the rolling 24h staging run; crossing the gate requires all\n"
"four targets, not three-of-four.\n"
msgstr ""
"<!-- verified: 2026-04-17 · MDD × Paddock · pre-release SLI gate -->\n"
"\n"
"# 发布 SLI 关卡\n"
"\n"
"一个候选发布版本在生产环境之外被拦住，直到以下这些 SLI 在 staging 的\n"
"一个滚动 24 小时窗口里都达到目标：\n"
"\n"
"| SLI                         | 目标           | 窗口  |\n"
"|-----------------------------|----------------|-------|\n"
"| p99 延迟（用户路径）         | ≤ 400 ms       | 24h   |\n"
"| 错误率                        | ≤ 0.1 %        | 24h   |\n"
"| 挽具内部成本／轮             | ≤ $0.03        | 24h   |\n"
"| 规约 vs. 生产漂移分          | ≤ 2 条发现     | 24h   |\n"
"\n"
"牧场就是这段滚动 24 小时的 staging 运行；要过这道关，四条目标全部要过，\n"
"不接受四过三。\n"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:341
#: 46f1e96768de470394de7e2f290253fe
msgid "MDD × Groom — Weekly metric audits and dashboard hygiene"
msgstr "MDD × 梳理 —— 每周度量审计与仪表盘卫生"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:343
#: 5c4a49d3c9c741f0bbfc60be21749e8c
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Definition.** A groom action in this cell is a *weekly review of the "
"metric surface itself* — which signals are still steering decisions, which "
"dashboards have no owner, which alerts fire without a runbook. Lehman's laws"
" {cite}`lehman1980laws` apply to metrics as much as to code: unmaintained "
"signals decay into noise."
msgstr ""
"**定义。** 这一格里的梳理动作，是一场 *每周对度量面本身的复盘*——哪些信号还在真正引导决策、哪些仪表盘已经没有 owner、哪些告警在没有 "
"runbook 的情况下就会触发。Lehman 的演化律 {cite}`lehman1980laws` "
"对度量的适用度与对代码一样：没人维护的信号，会衰减成噪声。"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:349
#: 2d71d626104d453b9f9d0f46e2756b8a
#, python-format
msgid ""
"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n"
"# verified: 2026-04-17 · MDD × Groom · weekly audit that tends the metric surface\n"
"# Not \"collect more metrics\" — prune stale ones and verify the living ones\n"
"# still steer something.\n"
"set -euo pipefail\n"
"\n"
"echo \"== metrics retention ==\"\n"
"python scripts/audit_metrics.py --older-than 90d --action list-unused\n"
"\n"
"echo \"== dashboard coverage ==\"\n"
"python scripts/audit_dashboards.py --require-owner --require-runbook\n"
"\n"
"echo \"== cost trend ==\"\n"
"python scripts/cost_trend.py --since \"$(date -d '7 days ago' +%F)\"\n"
"\n"
"echo \"write the findings to metrics-review-$(date +%F).md and open a PR\"\n"
msgstr ""
"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n"
"# verified: 2026-04-17 · MDD × Groom · weekly audit that tends the metric surface\n"
"# Not \"collect more metrics\" — prune stale ones and verify the living ones\n"
"# still steer something.\n"
"set -euo pipefail\n"
"\n"
"echo \"== metrics retention ==\"\n"
"python scripts/audit_metrics.py --older-than 90d --action list-unused\n"
"\n"
"echo \"== dashboard coverage ==\"\n"
"python scripts/audit_dashboards.py --require-owner --require-runbook\n"
"\n"
"echo \"== cost trend ==\"\n"
"python scripts/cost_trend.py --since \"$(date -d '7 days ago' +%F)\"\n"
"\n"
"echo \"write the findings to metrics-review-$(date +%F).md and open a PR\"\n"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:353
#: 60e4b99fa63649c08c6239f4d89dcc53
msgid "Pitfall — MDD row failure modes"
msgstr "陷阱——MDD 行的失败模式"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:356
#: 9445f33a9acb4140ab9e492fd5d0c6c5
msgid ""
"The MDD row fails more quietly than the other two rows because metrics decay"
" *asymptotically*: a broken test goes red, a stale spec produces obvious "
"contradictions, but a decaying dashboard merely becomes less useful. The "
"three row-level failures:"
msgstr ""
"MDD 行失败得比另外两行更安静，因为度量的衰减是 *渐近* "
"的：坏掉的测试会红、过期的规约会产出明显的矛盾，而一块正在衰减的仪表盘，只是变得越来越不管用。三种行级失败："

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:361
#: 24ba276e18d14dcdabe075834dd8a926
msgid ""
"**The north-star nobody watches.** A metric was declared load-bearing, a "
"dashboard was built, a threshold was set — and no one looks at it outside "
"incidents. The signal exists but does not *steer*; MDD × Bridle has a file "
"and an empty chair. Fix: every north-star needs a named owner and a weekly "
"agenda slot, or demote it to a diagnostic."
msgstr ""
"**没人盯的北极星。** 一条度量被宣布承重、一块仪表盘被搭起来、一个阈值被设上——然后除了事故时以外没人看。信号在，但它不 *引导*；MDD × "
"缰绳这一格，有文件，有空椅子。**解法**：每一条北极星都必须有一位署名 owner，和每周一个议程格子，否则就把它降级为诊断度量。"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:367
#: fdd6e3b8dfb94ab191b3fdddc2ef0557
msgid ""
"**The cost cap with no tripwire.** A cost cap is configured at the API layer"
" and never fires. Either the cap is too loose (it silently permits "
"regression) or the cap is tight enough to matter but nobody is paged when it"
" hits. MDD × Fence that never refuses anything for a quarter is "
"indistinguishable from no fence at all."
msgstr ""
"**没有绊线的成本上限。** 在 API "
"层配了一条成本上限，它从不触发。要么这条上限太松（它沉默地放行了回归），要么它紧到值得关心、却没人在它命中时被呼叫。MDD × "
"护栏若整整一个季度都没拒绝过任何东西，和\"没有护栏\"没有区别。"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:373
#: ad363ca7df13439d91c7b063b80e8639
msgid ""
"**The SLI that drifted from reality.** The staging SLI still measures "
"endpoint P99, but the product shifted last quarter and the load-bearing path"
" is now a background job whose latency the SLI ignores. Release gates keep "
"passing; regressions ship. MDD × Paddock demands the SLIs be re-audited "
"whenever the product's load-bearing path moves — which the agent's velocity "
"now makes more frequent, not less."
msgstr ""
"**与现实脱节的 SLI。** staging 的 SLI 仍然在量端点的 P99，但产品上个季度转了向，真正的承重路径已经变成一个后台作业，而这条 "
"SLI 恰好忽略了它的延迟。发布关卡一路都在过；回归照样上线。MDD × 牧场要求：每当产品的承重路径发生位移，SLI "
"就必须被重新审计——而智能体的速度，让这种位移变得 *更* 频繁，不是更少。"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:381
#: 690c8ccf1f5748749ed50f82801f35cf
msgid ""
"Row-level test: for each MDD cell, can you name both the signal *and* the "
"specific decision it drove in the last thirty days? A signal without a "
"decision it influenced is a dashboard pixel, not a guardian."
msgstr ""
"行级自测：针对 MDD 的每一格，你都能点出 *既有* 那条信号、*也有* "
"它在过去三十天内驱动的某一项具体决定吗？一条没有驱动任何决定的信号，是仪表盘上的一个像素，而不是一位护法。"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:387
#: b14d511004b844ee960a3cc60c1b96da
msgid "Research Foundations"
msgstr "研究脉络"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:389
#: a27436c5417b45549f9f7c4a9c6eabf9
msgid "The matrix's analytical claim rests on five citable pillars:"
msgstr "这张矩阵的分析主张，靠五根可引用的支柱支着："

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:391
#: ed8caa2675ce47219cee61b5094713c6
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Primary academic source** for Harness Engineering as a distinct "
"discipline: the CAR decomposition and HarnessCard reporting format "
"{cite}`car2025decomposition`."
msgstr ""
"**首要学术来源**：把 Harness Engineering 作为一门独立学科对待——CAR 分解与 HarnessCard 报告格式 "
"{cite}`car2025decomposition`。"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:394
#: 398250242dd94fb48d66de1f2ad58d3a
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Industry triangulation** across two independent, non-academic framings: "
"Thoughtworks' radar entry {cite}`thoughtworks2026harness` and LangChain's "
"five-part anatomy {cite}`langchain2026tbench`."
msgstr ""
"**业界三点定位**：两份独立、非学术的框法——Thoughtworks 技术雷达的条目 "
"{cite}`thoughtworks2026harness`、以及 LangChain 的五段式解剖 "
"{cite}`langchain2026tbench`。"

#: ../../source/chapters/05-harness-anatomy.md:397
#: cf46eef3cb084b0b8934596f0f795f2c
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Fitness-function lineage** for the zones: Ford, Parsons & Kua's *Building "
"Evolutionary Architectures* {cite}`ford2017buildingevolutionary` supplies "
"the vocabulary of *architectural fitness functions* the four zones "
"operationalise."
msgstr ""
